        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "486cb1dd-28a0-5cd3-bf02-3f3c8a635cce",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Bo Diddley, Paul Samwell-Smith, Elvis Presley, Buddy Holly, Eric Clapton, Jimi Hendrix, George Thorogood, Jeff Beck, Jimmy Page\n- Bands: The Yardbirds, the Beatles, the Rolling Stones, the Who, Parliament-Funkadelic, The Clash\n- Songs: \"Before You Accuse Me\"\n- Places: London, Richmond, Surrey\n- Topics: rock and roll, blues, R&B\n\nFacts:\n- Bo Diddley was born as Ellas Otha Bates on December 30, 1928, and he was later known as Ellas McDaniel.\n- Bo Diddley wrote and recorded the song \"Before You Accuse Me\" in 1957.\n- The Yardbirds formed in London in 1963 as an English rock band.\n- Paul Samwell-Smith was born as Paul Smith on May 8, 1943, in Richmond, Surrey.\n- Paul Samwell-Smith became best known as a founding member and bassist of The Yardbirds.\n- The Yardbirds became associated with notable musicians including Jeff Beck, Eric Clapton, and Jimmy Page.\n- Bo Diddley was an American R&B singer, guitarist, songwriter, and music producer who played a key role in the transition from blues to rock and roll.\n- Bo Diddley influenced artists including Elvis Presley, Buddy Holly, the Beatles, the Rolling Stones, the Yardbirds, Eric Clapton, the Who, Jimi Hendrix, George Thorogood, Parliament-Funkadelic, and The Clash.\n- Bo Diddley died on June 2, 2008.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
